        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor(qa): add canonical live channel adapters",
        "body": "Closes #99699\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nTelegram, Slack, WhatsApp, and Matrix live QA runtimes cannot currently be selected by the shared QA Lab scenario host. Matrix also lives in its own QA runner plugin, so QA Lab needs an owner-neutral way to discover its transport adapter without importing plugin-private code.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nEach channel now contributes a canonical `QaTransportAdapterFactory` through its existing QA runner registration. QA Lab discovers those factories through the existing runner contribution seam and can run shared scenarios with `qa suite --channel-driver live --channel <adapter-id>`.\n\nThe existing `qa telegram`, `qa slack`, `qa whatsapp`, and `qa matrix` commands keep their current runners and scenario catalogs. This provides a migration target for shared YAML/flow scenarios without changing shipped defaults, scenario ids, Matrix profiles, artifacts, cleanup, or forced-exit behavior.\n\nNo hosted adapter union, parallel runtime factory, second registry, capability manifest, or recorder polling is introduced.\n\n## User Impact\n\nExisting live QA commands behave as before. Maintainers can begin migrating shared scenarios to the canonical adapters one channel at a time, then remove each legacy scenario runner only after its command contract is fully represented by the shared host.\n\nExplicit shared live-adapter runs are host-only, use one worker, reject runtime-pair duplication, and default to the selected factory's declared canonical scenarios.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Rebased onto `6c53dfa1df99ef82d8d25600f809b1296176c4e0`.\n- Focused SDK, discovery, adapter, shared-host, preserved CLI, and Matrix substrate proof passed 188 tests after rebase.\n- Additional affected-path proof passed 118 tests after forwarding effective scenario selections.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- Final Codex autoreview is clean with no accepted/actionable findings (0.97 confidence).\n- Extension production/test type lanes currently encounter unrelated current-main Telegram `UserFromGetMe` and Workboard `StatsFs` errors outside this PR; focused touched-surface type and runtime proof is green.\n- Exact-content Testbox rerun `tbx_01kwqb7xsqdzn1dcn55tmb7xsr` passed all type lanes and core lint, then identified task-owned adapter lint findings; those findings were fixed and the exact changed adapter files now pass the extension lint command locally. The first run `tbx_01kwqa75s0tn4e56vqrvy2mc25` was cancelled during delegated runner cleanup with no code assertion.\n",
        "branch": "dallin/wave1-channel-host",
